WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.117
What happens when the amount is bigger than one whole?

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:07.709
Today we are exploring mixed numbers and improper fractions.

00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:13.869
We will build the wholes, count the extra pieces, and connect two ways of naming exactly the same amount.

00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:15.920
Ready to investigate?

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.637
Four quarters make one whole.

00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:21.486
Another four quarters make a second whole.

00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:23.716
Three quarters are left over.

00:00:24.366 --> 00:00:27.263
Eleven quarters is an improper fraction.

00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:30.918
Its numerator is at least as large as its denominator.

00:00:31.138 --> 00:00:33.370
It can describe one whole or more.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.559
Two and three quarters is a mixed number.

00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:39.911
It combines two whole units with a fractional part.

00:00:40.561 --> 00:00:43.278
To convert, divide eleven by four.

00:00:43.498 --> 00:00:47.263
Eleven divided by four is two with a remainder of three.

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:51.881
The denominator stays four because our pieces are still quarters.

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:55.382
So eleven quarters equals two and three quarters.

00:00:56.032 --> 00:00:57.737
Now go the other way.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.084
Take three and two fifths.

00:01:00.304 --> 00:01:02.896
Each whole contains five fifths.

00:01:03.546 --> 00:01:06.258
Three times five gives fifteen fifths.

00:01:06.478 --> 00:01:09.978
Add the extra two fifths to make seventeen fifths.

00:01:10.628 --> 00:01:14.228
So three and two fifths equals seventeen fifths.

00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:19.532
Multiply the whole number by the denominator, add the numerator, and keep the denominator.

00:01:20.182 --> 00:01:23.132
A fraction can also equal an exact whole.

00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:27.300
Eight quarters is two wholes, with no fractional part left over.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:31.113
To compare mixed numbers, compare the wholes first.

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:35.004
Three and one quarter is greater than two and three quarters.

00:01:35.654 --> 00:01:38.666
If the wholes match, compare the fractional parts.

00:01:38.886 --> 00:01:42.198
Two and one half is greater than two and one quarter.

00:01:42.848 --> 00:01:45.834
How many wholes and quarters are in nine quarters?

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:52.861
Nine quarters is two wholes and one quarter.

00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:58.883
Group equal fractional parts to make wholes, then keep the remainder as a fraction.

00:01:59.103 --> 00:02:03.669
Mixed numbers and improper fractions are two ways to name the same amount.
